IMPORT prelude

-- Hire-Purchase Act 1969 (Singapore) -- which agreements the Act regulates (s 2, First Schedule), when the owner may enforce one
-- (s 5), the hirer's right to a copy and a statement (s 8), assignment (s 11), termination by returning the goods (s 14),
-- repossession and what follows it (ss 15-17), guarantee agreements needing a solicitor (s 21), excessive terms charges (s 29),
-- reopening a harsh transaction (s 32(5)), void clauses (s 33), secondhand goods (s 39) and the offences (ss 35-37, 48).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HPA1969.txt. The cover says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The last amending Act in the
-- deposited legislative history is Act 11 of 2013 (Insurance (Amendment) Act 2013). SSO's metadata calls it the "Current version
-- as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it governs buying a car or household goods on instalments, and what happens
-- when a payment is missed and the goods are taken back. SCOPED to the provisions a hirer or guarantor meets. Not encoded: the
-- implied terms as to title, description and quality (Part 3, ss 6-6G), misrepresentation (s 7), appropriation of payments (s 9),
-- removal of goods (s 10), the owner's assignment (s 11A), early completion (s 13), regaining the goods (s 18), the guarantor's other
-- rights (ss 20, 22-24), insurance (Part 6), workers' liens, fixtures, service of notices, the ten-point type rule (s 47), and
-- anything prescribed by regulations (terms-charge caps, overdue-interest caps, fees), none of which was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 -- hirers`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- regulated agreements`

-- s 2(1): "regulated agreement" means a hire-purchase or conditional sale agreement "which relates to the goods specified in the
-- First Schedule, but does not include any agreement in which the hirer is engaged in the trade or business of selling goods of the
-- same nature or description".
-- First Schedule: 1. "Any consumer goods the value of which does not exceed $20,000 (inclusive of any goods and services tax)".
-- 2(2). On or after 15 July 1994, "any motor vehicle the value of which does not exceed $55,000", including GST and import and
-- excise duty, "but shall exclude the cost of a certificate of entitlement". 3. "consumer goods" means goods purchased "for
-- personal, family or household purposes and not for the purposes of any trade or business".
-- Item 2 does not say the vehicle must be for personal use; the encoding reads it that way (an inference from the text).
DECLARE Goods IS ONE OF
    `consumer goods`
    `a motor vehicle`
    `goods bought for a business`

GIVEN `the goods` IS A Goods, `the price including GST and duty` IS A NUMBER, `the COE cost` IS A NUMBER,
      `the hirer trades in such goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is regulated` IF
        (NOT `the hirer trades in such goods`)
    AND CONSIDER `the goods`
        WHEN `consumer goods` THEN `the price including GST and duty` AT MOST 20000
        WHEN `a motor vehicle` THEN `the price including GST and duty` MINUS `the COE cost` AT MOST 55000
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5 -- when the owner may enforce`

-- s 5(1): "A regulated agreement that is not in writing shall not be enforceable by the owner."
-- (2): the owner may not enforce the agreement, a guarantee or any right to recover the goods "unless the requirements set out in
-- sections 3(3)(b) to (e) and 4 have been complied with" (signature, particulars, the tabular price statement; a copy and the Third
-- Schedule notice served within 7 business days).
-- (3): "Notwithstanding subsection (2)", the court may dispense with requirements of ss 3 and 4 if the failure "has not prejudiced
-- the hirer" and it is "just and equitable". Subsection (3) overrides (2) only; it says nothing of (1).
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed with the required particulars` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `copy and notice served in 7 business days` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court dispenses with the defect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may enforce the agreement` IF
        `in writing`
    AND (    (`signed with the required particulars` AND `copy and notice served in 7 business days`)
         OR  `the court dispenses with the defect`)

§§ `8 -- copy of the agreement and statement of account`

-- s 8(1): the owner shall, "within 7 business days", comply with a hirer's written request, made "at any time before final
-- payment", for a copy of the agreement or a signed statement of amounts paid, due and to become payable.
-- (2): the owner need not comply (a) "if he has sent the hirer the document requested within a period of 3 months immediately
-- preceding the request"; or (b) for a second or later request for a copy of the agreement, "unless the request is accompanied by
-- a reasonable fee". (3): while a failure without reasonable cause continues, the owner may not enforce the agreement, recover the
-- goods or enforce a guarantee.
-- The exact 3-month boundary is not tested.
GIVEN `final payment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since that document was last sent` IS A NUMBER,
      `a repeat request for a copy of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable fee is enclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner must answer the request` IF
        (NOT `final payment has been made`)
    AND `months since that document was last sent` GREATER THAN 3
    AND ((NOT `a repeat request for a copy of the agreement`) OR `a reasonable fee is enclosed`)

§§ `11 -- assigning the hirer's rights`

-- s 11(1): the hirer's interest "may be assigned with the consent of the owner, or if his consent is unreasonably withheld, without
-- his consent". (2): where an owner "requires any such payment or other consideration for his consent, that consent shall be deemed
-- to be unreasonably withheld" (save the defaults and reasonable costs of s 11(5)).
GIVEN `the owner consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner demands payment for consent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the refusal is otherwise unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hirer may assign` IF
        `the owner consents`
    OR  `the owner demands payment for consent`
    OR  `the refusal is otherwise unreasonable`

§§ `14 -- terminating by returning the goods`

-- s 14(1): the hirer "may terminate the hiring by returning the goods to the owner". (6): the owner may then recover "(a) the amount
-- (if any) required to be paid in those circumstances under the agreement; or (b) the amount (if any) that the owner would have been
-- entitled to recover if he had taken possession of the goods at the date of termination ... whichever is less".
GIVEN `the amount under the agreement` IS A NUMBER, `the amount had the owner repossessed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the owner recovers on the hirer's termination` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `the amount under the agreement` `the amount had the owner repossessed`

§§ `15(1), (2) -- notice before repossession`

-- s 15(1): for a breach "relating to the payment of instalments", the owner shall not take possession "until he has served on the
-- hirer a notice, in writing, in the form set out in the Fourth Schedule and the period fixed by the notice has expired, which shall
-- not be less than 7 business days after the service of the notice".
-- (2): not needed if there are "reasonable grounds for believing that the goods ... will be removed or concealed by the hirer", but
-- "the onus of proving the existence of those grounds shall lie upon the owner".
-- A notice fixing fewer than 7 days is read as still requiring 7 to pass (an inference; the text could also be read as making the
-- notice invalid).
GIVEN `Fourth Schedule notice served` IS A BOOLEAN, `days fixed by the notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `business days since service` IS A NUMBER, `the owner proves a risk of removal or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may repossess for missed instalments` IF
        `the owner proves a risk of removal or concealment`
    OR  (    `Fourth Schedule notice served`
         AND `business days since service` AT LEAST `the greater of` `days fixed by the notice` 7)

§§ `15(3), (6) -- notice after repossession`

-- s 15(3): "Within 7 business days after the owner has taken possession", he shall serve on the hirer and every guarantor the Fifth
-- Schedule notice. (6): "If the notice required by subsection (3) is not served, the rights of the owner under the regulated
-- agreement shall thereupon cease and determine."
GIVEN `Fifth Schedule notice served` IS A BOOLEAN, `business days after repossession when served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner keeps his rights after repossession` IF
    `Fifth Schedule notice served` AND `business days after repossession when served` AT MOST 7

§§ `16 -- the owner must hold the goods`

-- s 16: the owner shall not, "without the written consent of the hirer", sell, dispose of or part with the goods "(a) until after the
-- expiration of 7 business days after the date of the service on the hirer of the notice referred to in section 15(3); or (b) if
-- notice under section 17(1)(a) has been given, until the time for payment or tender pursuant to that notice has expired, whichever
-- is the later".
GIVEN `the hirer consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `business days since the Fifth Schedule notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `the hirer asked for the goods back or a sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `the hirer's time to pay has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may sell the repossessed goods` IF
        `the hirer consents in writing`
    OR  (    `business days since the Fifth Schedule notice` GREATER THAN 7
         AND ((NOT `the hirer asked for the goods back or a sale`) OR `the hirer's time to pay has expired`))

§§ `17 -- the hirer's refund and the cap on the owner's claim`

-- s 17(3): the value of the goods is "the best price that could be reasonably obtained by the owner at that time" (or what a buyer
-- introduced by the hirer paid), less the costs of taking possession, storage, repair or maintenance, and selling.
-- (1)(b): the hirer may recover (i) where value is less than the "net amount payable" but value plus what the hirer paid exceeds it,
-- "the difference between that total and the net amount payable"; (ii) where value is at least the net amount payable, "the total of
-- that value and the amount paid ... less the net amount payable". Both limbs come to the same sum: value plus paid, less the net
-- amount payable.
-- (2): the owner "is not entitled to recover any sum" which, added to the value and the amount paid, "exceeds the net amount
-- payable". "Net amount payable" is not defined in s 2 of this edition; it is an input here.
GIVEN `best price` IS A NUMBER, `repossession costs` IS A NUMBER, `storage and repair costs` IS A NUMBER,
      `selling expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the repossessed goods` MEANS
    `best price` MINUS `repossession costs` MINUS `storage and repair costs` MINUS `selling expenses`

GIVEN `goods value` IS A NUMBER, `amount the hirer paid` IS A NUMBER, `net amount payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hirer's refund` MEANS
    IF `goods value` PLUS `amount the hirer paid` GREATER THAN `net amount payable`
    THEN `goods value` PLUS `amount the hirer paid` MINUS `net amount payable`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `goods value` IS A NUMBER, `amount the hirer paid` IS A NUMBER, `net amount payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the owner may still recover` MEANS
    IF `net amount payable` GREATER THAN `goods value` PLUS `amount the hirer paid`
    THEN `net amount payable` MINUS `goods value` MINUS `amount the hirer paid`
    ELSE 0

-- s 17(5): "No amount is recoverable by the hirer under this section except where the owner has failed to serve" the s 15(3) notice
-- unless (a) the hirer, "within 7 business days after the owner has served" it, gives written notice of the amount claimed and the
-- value claimed; and (b) proceedings are commenced "not later than 3 months after" that notice.
GIVEN `the owner served the Fifth Schedule notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `business days to the hirer's claim notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `months from claim notice to proceedings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hirer can still claim the refund` IF
        (NOT `the owner served the Fifth Schedule notice`)
    OR  (`business days to the hirer's claim notice` AT MOST 7 AND `months from claim notice to proceedings` AT MOST 3)

§§ `21 -- guarantees that need a solicitor`

-- s 21(1): a guarantor's agreement binding him "(a) to pay to the owner an aggregate sum which is larger than the balance originally
-- payable under the agreement; or (b) to perform an obligation in respect of goods other than the goods comprised in the regulated
-- agreement" is "void unless the agreement is executed by the guarantor in the presence of a solicitor instructed and employed
-- independently of the owner and the solicitor certifies in writing" that the guarantor understands it and executed it in his
-- presence.
GIVEN `the guarantee exceeds the balance originally payable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the guarantee covers other goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an independent solicitor certified it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guarantee agreement is void` IF
        (`the guarantee exceeds the balance originally payable` OR `the guarantee covers other goods`)
    AND (NOT `an independent solicitor certified it`)

§§ `29 -- terms charges above the prescribed cap`

-- s 29(1): terms charges "shall not exceed such amount as may be prescribed". (2): if they do, the hirer may by signed written notice
-- "elect either to treat the agreement as void or to have his liability reduced by the amount included in the agreement for terms
-- charges" -- the whole terms charges, not only the excess. (3): if void, everything the hirer paid "shall be recoverable by action as
-- a debt". The prescribed cap is in regulations not retrieved; it is an input.
DECLARE Election IS ONE OF
    `treat the agreement as void`
    `reduce the liability`

GIVEN `the election` IS A Election, `the hirer's remaining liability` IS A NUMBER, `the terms charges` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the hirer still owes after electing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the election`
    WHEN `treat the agreement as void` THEN 0
    WHEN `reduce the liability` THEN `the hirer's remaining liability` MINUS `the terms charges`

GIVEN `the election` IS A Election, `the amount the hirer has paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`what the hirer recovers as a debt on electing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the election`
    WHEN `treat the agreement as void` THEN `the amount the hirer has paid`
    WHEN `reduce the liability` THEN 0

§§ `32(5) -- time to ask the court to reopen a harsh transaction`

-- s 32(1): the court may reopen a transaction that "is harsh and unconscionable". (4) the hirer or a guarantor may sue for that
-- relief, but (5) not "(a) ... where the owner has taken possession of the goods ... after the expiration of a period of 4 months
-- after the date on which the owner serves" the s 15(3) notice; "(b) in any other case, after the expiration of a period of 4 months
-- from the time when the transaction is closed". The exact 4-month boundary is not tested.
GIVEN `months since the notice or the closing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hirer may still apply to reopen` IF
    `months since the notice or the closing` AT MOST 4

§§ `33 -- clauses that are void`

-- s 33: void "and of no effect" is any provision whereby (a) a right of the hirer to determine the agreement is excluded or restricted;
-- (b) the hirer bears a greater liability on determination than under the Act; (c) interest on overdue instalments exceeds the rate
-- prescribed by the Minister; (d) "the owner is relieved from liability for the acts or defaults of any person acting in connection
-- with" the negotiations; (e) entry on premises to repossess otherwise than under the Act; (f) termination or repossession "if the
-- hirer becomes bankrupt"; (g) the Act is excluded, modified or restricted.
-- The Act itself contemplates clauses requiring insurance at the hirer's expense (s 25), forbidding liens (s 40(2)) and fixing where
-- the goods are kept (s 10); those are not void.
DECLARE Clause IS ONE OF
    `the hirer may not return the goods early`
    `repossession if the hirer becomes bankrupt`
    `the owner may enter the hirer's home to repossess at will`
    `the owner is not liable for the dealer's statements`
    `overdue interest above the prescribed rate`
    `the goods must be insured at the hirer's expense`
    `the hirer may not create a lien`
    `the goods must be kept at the hirer's address`

GIVEN `the clause` IS A Clause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause is void` IF
    CONSIDER `the clause`
    WHEN `the goods must be insured at the hirer's expense` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the hirer may not create a lien` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the goods must be kept at the hirer's address` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `39 -- secondhand goods not described as secondhand`

-- s 39(1): where the goods are secondhand, then unless "(a) the goods are described in the agreement as secondhand goods; or (b)" in
-- the owner's enforcement proceedings the court is satisfied that "(i) the hirer was aware" or "(ii) the owner was not aware" that they
-- were secondhand, "the liability of the hirer under the agreement shall be reduced by the amount included in the agreement for terms
-- charges".
GIVEN `the goods are secondhand` IS A BOOLEAN, `described as secondhand` IS A BOOLEAN, `the hirer knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the owner did not know` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the terms charges come off the hirer's liability` IF
        `the goods are secondhand`
    AND (NOT `described as secondhand`)
    AND (NOT `the hirer knew`)
    AND (NOT `the owner did not know`)

§§ `35-37, 27(2), 44(3), 48 -- offences`

-- s 35: a dealer or owner's agent who knowingly puts a materially false statement in an agreement or offer: "a fine not exceeding
-- $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both". s 36(2): a hirer who does not say where the goods are
-- within 7 business days of a notice, or knowingly answers falsely: $5,000 or 12 months. s 37: defrauding the owner by disposing of,
-- selling or removing the goods: $5,000 or "3 years". s 27(2): knowingly paying an insurance rebate to an owner, and s 44(3): not
-- obeying a delivery order, carry no penalty of their own, so s 48 applies: "$3,000 or ... 12 months or to both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `a dealer's false statement in the agreement`
    `a hirer not saying where the goods are`
    `a hirer fraudulently disposing of the goods`
    `paying an insurance rebate to the owner`
    `disobeying a court delivery order`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a dealer's false statement in the agreement` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a hirer not saying where the goods are` THEN 5000
    WHEN `a hirer fraudulently disposing of the goods` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 3000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a hirer fraudulently disposing of the goods` THEN 36
    OTHERWISE 12
